.TH EXTRUDE 1
.SH NAME
extrude \- make solids from outlines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B extrude
.IR part | \-
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Extrude
reads a part source or a stream and writes a stream on the standard
output, with a solid added for each
.B extrude
statement, and with the ranges of their faces: for each parameter of
a range that the solids lean on
.RI ( plicad (7)),
it makes them again with the parameter moved and writes where each
end of the range moves each face
.RI ( stream (5)).
.BR Profile ,
.B corner
and
.B circle
statements give the outlines.
Other statements are passed on.
The statements are described in
.IR part (5).
.SH EXAMPLES
extrude box.part | bool \- | fillet \- | tostep \- >box.step
.SH SEE ALSO
part(5), stream(5), bool(1), fillet(1), tostep(1)
